        "content": "<p>SebTardif opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14135\">PR #14135</a> from <code>SebTardif:fix/dir-read-is-directory</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Prior discussion: <a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc/pull/869#pullrequestreview-4931921277\">WebAssembly/wasi-libc#869</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">@alexcrichton</a>: fix this in Wasmtime instead of extra libc syscalls).</p>\n<h2>Why</h2>\n<p><code>read()</code> on a directory must return <code>EISDIR</code> (POSIX). Wasmtime's <code>Descriptor::file()</code> mapped a directory to <code>error-code::bad-descriptor</code>. wasi-libc then had to <code>stat</code>/<code>get_type</code> just to remap <code>EBADF</code>. On wasip3, <code>read-via-stream</code> is a tuple import, so that host <code>?</code> trapped instead of returning a guest error.</p>\n<p><code>wasi:filesystem</code> already documents <code>is-directory</code> as the <code>EISDIR</code> analog. <code>Descriptor::dir()</code> already returns <code>not-directory</code> for a file. This makes <code>file()</code> the dual.</p>\n<h2>Change</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Descriptor::file()</code> returns <code>IsDirectory</code> for <code>Dir</code>.</li>\n<li>wasip3 <code>read-via-stream</code>: if the descriptor is not a file, return an empty stream and resolve the result future with that error (same shape as p3 TCP receive). Do not trap.</li>\n<li>wasip1 guests are unchanged (<code>fd_read</code> still <code>EBADF</code>; preview1 adapter still <code>ERRNO_BADF</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Tests</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>p2_file_read_write</code>: <code>read_via_stream</code> on the preopen directory is <code>is-directory</code>.</li>\n<li><code>p3_filesystem_file_read_write</code>: the result future is <code>IsDirectory</code> (blocking and non-blocking).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Red (unpatched host): p2 guest saw <code>bad-descriptor</code> (code 3). Green: <code>is-directory</code> (code 14).</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc/pull/869\">WebAssembly/wasi-libc#869</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-libc/issues/865\">WebAssembly/wasi-libc#865</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/160359\">rust-lang/rust#160359</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/uutils/coreutils/issues/13625\">uutils/coreutils#13625</a></li>\n<li><code>Descriptor::file</code> as used today was introduced in <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/11406\">#11406</a> (<code>cf88a7c601</code>, 2025-08-12)<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
